Ladybird measures an absolutely positioned box’s intrinsic inline sizes
with the definite block size established by its opposing insets. The
percentage basis includes margin, border, and padding deductions and
its definite minimum and maximum block-size limits. Content-dependent
block sizes remain indefinite during that intrinsic measurement.

Blink’s ComputeOofInlineDimensions passes the inset-modified available
size and block auto-size behavior to BlockNode::ComputeMinMaxSizes.
Its intrinsic sizing consequently uses the stretched block size as
its descendant percentage basis. Gecko’s ComputeAbsolutePosAutoSize
resolves the stretch-fit block size before calling ShrinkISizeToFit,
passing the result through ComputeBSizeValueAsPercentageBasis to apply
its definite minimum and maximum limits.

WebKit derives the intrinsic width from the resolved height in its
RenderReplaced::computeAspectRatioAdjustedIntrinsicLogicalWidths.
RenderReplaced::computeReplacedLogicalHeightUsingGeneric and RenderBox::
availableLogicalHeightUsing obtain an auto-height positioned ancestor’s
height from computeLogicalHeight when both block insets are specified.
Ladybird follows the same behavior without resolving content-dependent
heights from the width that is being measured.
